    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following the spec's seven rules, keeping the given signature and the `CouponError` class. Item validation runs first, then the subtotal is summed. Coupon validity is checked in the spec's order (expiry, used code, minimum subtotal, kind), and percent and fixed value checks follow. Shipping is decided on the post-discount subtotal, with no shipping for an empty item list. The result is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I wrote 30 pytest cases in `tests/test_solution.py` covering the boundaries (expiry day, minimum subtotal, exactly 100.00 for free shipping, discount capped at subtotal, halves rounding) and the error paths. I ran `python -m pytest -q tests` and all 30 passed. One judgement call: I reject `bool` as a quantity even though Python treats it as an int.",
